<h2 class="doc-h2">Invalid</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    A setting that cannot be turned on until something else is true is a validation failure, not a
    disabled control — and saying so is better than silently refusing.
</p>
<Example Source="SwitchInvalid.razor"><SwitchInvalid /></Example>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Choice Card</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    The whole card is the label, so the entire panel is the hit target, and the state is legible
    from the border because <code>has-[:checked]</code> reads the input rather than a copy of it.
</p>
<Example Source="SwitchChoiceCard.razor"><SwitchChoiceCard /></Example>

